## Documentation discipline

Every meaningful change updates documentation in the **same edit batch** as the code change:

- `STATE.md` — overwrite affected sections.
- `CHANGELOG.md` — append, never edit.
- `CLIENT_DOCS.md` — when behaviour visible to the client changes.
- `PROJECT_MAP.md` — when structure changes.
- `RELEASE_NOTES.md` — at release time.
- `LESSONS.md` — after ANY user correction: acknowledge, fix, then append a lesson (pattern + root cause + preventive rule) BEFORE continuing. See `PROJECT_RULES.md` §3.1.

## The `/atomic-prompts` skill

If the user asks for an atomic prompt (via `/atomic-prompts` or by naming the skill), do **not** implement the idea inline. Instead, run the skill at `.claude/skills/atomic-prompts/SKILL.md` which generates `atomic-prompts/NNNN-<slug>.md`. Print path and acceptance-criteria count, then stop.

## Forbidden

- Destructive shell commands without explicit confirmation.
- Committing on behalf of the user unless asked.
- "Improving" code outside the request.
- Editing CHANGELOG.md retroactively.
- Writing to `templates/` (should not exist post-interview).

## Testing policy

<<#IF_TDD_NONE>>
Tests not required for this project. If adding tests later, update `CODING_RULES.md` first.
<</#IF_TDD_NONE>>
<<#IF_TDD_BASIC>>
Write test stubs alongside new code. Every new function should have at least one happy-path test before the feature is marked done.
<</#IF_TDD_BASIC>>
<<#IF_TDD_FULL>>
**Full TDD enforced.** Write the failing test first (RED). Run it — must fail. Implement minimally (GREEN). Refactor. Coverage ≥ 80% before marking done. Never skip the RED step.
<</#IF_TDD_FULL>>

## Security non-negotiables

- NEVER hardcode secrets, API keys, or tokens. Use `.env` + `process.env`.
- NEVER commit `.env`. Commit `.env.example` only.
- Validate all user input at system boundaries. Never trust external data.
- Parameterised queries only — never string-concatenate SQL.
- If a secret lands in source, stop immediately and flag it.

## Hooks (automatic guard-rails)

`.claude/hooks/` runs automatically on every edit:
- **PreToolUse**: secret scanner + config-file protection.
- **PostToolUse**: TypeScript type check + console.log warning + doc-sync reminder.
- **Stop**: auto-formatter (Biome → Prettier fallback) + final TS check.

Do not disable hooks without explicit user instruction.

